  "ai_summary": "Suryodaya Petrochem Industries Pvt. Ltd., a chemical manufacturer with a TIV of INR 9.4 billion, has been conditionally approved for a new industrial property policy following a Senior Underwriter review. The risk is classified as high due to significant operational hazards, including the bulk storage of 480 KL of flammable solvents and exothermic chemical processes, coupled with critical safety gaps such as the absence of automated sprinkler systems and aged electrical wiring. Additionally, the facility faces substantial CAT exposure, specifically high flood risk due to its proximity to the Khari River and poor drainage. To mitigate these exposures, approval is contingent upon a mandatory electrical audit and rewiring, a formal fire safety improvement plan for sprinkler installation, and an increased deductible of INR 75,000,000 for flood and natural catastrophe perils. A 25% risk loading has been applied to the base rate to account for the elevated hazard profile.",
